# Bottom Navigation Layout Rules

Locked files: `src/components/BottomNav.tsx` and `src/components/bottom-nav.module.css`, rendered once as a **direct child of `<body>`** in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Do not add a second nav in pages.

- Do NOT `position: fixed` on `html`. Do NOT make `body` a flex column or `overflow-y: auto`.
- The tab bar is a **floating pill**, not a full-width flush bar. Geometry in `bottom-nav.module.css`: `position: fixed`, `left: 50%`, `transform: translateX(-50%)`, `width: 92%`, `max-width: 420px`, `height: 62px`, `border-radius: 9999px`, `bottom: max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 16px))`. Do not pin it with JS. Do not add Tailwind `pb-*` / `mb-*` / `pb-safe` on the nav.
- Do NOT hide the nav on route change.

Every route uses `PageShell` with `w-full min-h-full pb-[96px] pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)] bg-background`.
`PageHeader` is not sticky.
